   "about": "The memorandum assesses Japan’s economic condition under occupation and the prospects for self-support.",
   "summary": "Reviews agriculture, fishing, industry, finance, occupation reforms, stabilization measures, and the slow recovery of foreign trade. It argues that population growth and disrupted Asian markets make a large expansion of exports essential. It recommends easing occupation controls and giving Japanese authorities responsibility for solving these problems, while continuing American aid during the transition.",
